3,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,785,2701,37236,374,14764,304,264,5792,566,417,6113,11,6825,264,20189,6113,323,264,29136,42939,13,220,3555,374,279,6629,315,400,87,54876,304,12348,30,220,17399,697,4226,438,264,4185,19419,382,58,6405,921,474,23962,280,1958,1548,600,28,15,26,600,2651,22,26,3443,72,8,341,7633,14161,7,18,21,15,23019,14,22,10,24,15,29621,3741,7,18,21,15,6599,72,10,16,5620,22,10,24,15,1106,532,12670,362,284,5419,7,18,21,15,9,15,14,22,10,24,15,317,12670,434,284,5419,7,18,21,15,9,19,14,22,10,24,15,317,12670,479,284,5419,7,18,21,15,9,20,14,22,10,24,15,317,12670,472,284,5419,7,18,21,15,9,21,14,22,10,24,15,626,7633,4346,313,37,626,3987,4044,56606,20912,87,73315,28442,7,15,13,20,5731,77,28,16,15883,4037,28,16,23,37306,27229,15031,626,24157,6405,60,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nThe following diagonal is drawn in a regular heptagon, creating a pentagon and a quadrilateral.  What is the measure of $x$, in degrees?  Express your answer as a common fraction.\n\n[asy]\nimport markers;\nfor(int i=0; i <=7; ++i) {\ndraw(dir(360*i/7+90)--dir(360*(i+1)/7+90));\n}\npair A = dir(360*0/7+90);\npair F = dir(360*4/7+90);\npair G = dir(360*5/7+90);\npair H = dir(360*6/7+90);\n\ndraw(A--F);\n\nmarkangle(Label(\"$x$\",Relative(0.5)),n=1,radius=18,G,F,A);\n\n[/asy]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"198d48fca402b3c74085fdd3e080b80c00a347cda50622f957b6dc08aa42b590"},"seconds":26.683608293533325,"seed":782394901763734913,"stop":"eos","text":"To find the measure of angle \\(x\\) in the given regular heptagon, we first need to understand that the interior angles of a regular heptagon each measure \\( \\frac{(7-2) \\times 180^\\circ}{7} = \\frac{5 \\times 180^\\circ}{7} = \\frac{900^\\circ}{7} \\).\n\nThe angle \\(x\\) is an exterior angle to the pentagon formed by drawing the diagonal in the heptagon. The pentagon has vertices that are part of the heptagon, so let's identify the angles involved.\n\nSince the heptagon is regular, each of its interior angles is \\( \\frac{900^\\circ}{7} \\). The angle \\(x\\) is the exterior angle of the pentagon formed by the diagonal and the sides of the heptagon. We need to find the measure of the interior angle of the pentagon at the vertex where the diagonal meets. This angle is the sum of two interior angles of the heptagon minus 180 degrees (since the diagonal splits the heptagon into two polygons).\n\nSo, the interior angle at this vertex of the pentagon is:\n\\[ 2 \\times \\frac{900^\\circ}{7} - 180^\\circ = \\frac{1800^\\circ}{7} - 180^\\circ = \\frac{1800^\\circ - 1260^\\circ}{7} = \\frac{540^\\circ}{7} \\]\n\nThe exterior angle \\(x\\) is the supplement of this interior angle of the pentagon:\n\\[ x = 180^\\circ - \\frac{540^\\circ}{7} = \\frac{1260^\\circ - 540^\\circ}{7} = \\frac{720^\\circ}{7} \\]\n\nTherefore, the measure of \\(x\\) in degrees is:\n\\[ \\boxed{\\frac{720}{7}} \\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\frac{720}{7}}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
